  "lineage": "Vietnamese đờn ca tài tử (\"music of talented amateurs\") southern-Vietnamese chamber-music tradition emerging in late-nineteenth-century Mekong Delta from the synthesis of the older nhã nhạc court-music tradition with southern-Vietnamese folk-music. UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage 2013. Performance configuration: small intimate amateur-ensemble of literate-class male and female musicians playing đàn tranh sixteen-string zither, đàn bầu one-string monochord, đàn nguyệt moon-lute, đàn tỳ bà pear-lute, đàn cò two-string fiddle, plus singer. Repertoire organized around the twenty bản tổ canonical melodic patterns. The form is the direct musical ancestor of cải lương southern-popular theatre.",
